{"title":"2016 JBMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e86b9fd6a0a9342a38aab17f93c5c92a6417e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB || CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/78045f207b8b1b88e062db9ba7d3563c6232981b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &gt; CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />) is circumscribed.The incircle of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> touches the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />,respectively.Prove that the incenter of the trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1#Solution\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be positive real numbers.Prove that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738b50c1464997293a7bc215a2b91ccd33e40b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{(a+b)^2 + 4abc} + \\frac{8}{(b+c)^2 + 4abc} + \\frac{8}{(a+c)^2 + 4abc} + a^2 + b^2 + c ^2 \\ge \\frac{8}{a+3} + \\frac{8}{b+3} + \\frac{8}{c+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"720\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2#Solution\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all triplets of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that the number\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496f7460105427895e3c88cb3d99ffadfb21bc41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\frac{(a-b)(b-c)(c-a)}{2} + 2\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"38\" />\n</pre>\n<p>is a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>(A power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer of form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfa2dc389103eac034705404f922458e2fa4edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />,where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a non-negative integer.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3#Solution\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197151a067f49bd4daa1952d1a4fac322409f0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> table is called regular f each of its cells contains one of four pairwise distinct real numbers,such that each of them occurs exactly one in every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> subtable.The sum of all numbers of a regular table is called the total sum of the table.With any four numbers,one constructs all possible regular tables,computes their total sums and counts the distinct outcomes.Determine the maximum possible count.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4#Solution\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO\" title=\"2016 JBMO\">2016 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 JBMO Problems\">2015 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 JBMO Problems\">2017 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061216\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.